{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941663-core-revelations-in-a-sentence","id":941663,"title":"Core Revelations in a Sentence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-01T21:06:32-07:00","id":941663,"title":"Core Revelations in a Sentence","content":"Here's a fun little exercise (that certainly has no ulterior motives, no sirree Bob):<br /> <br /> What is the key &quot;nugget&quot; of enlightenment for each Arcana? In other words, if you had to sum up the <i>idea</i> behind a given Arcana in a sentence, what would it be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T21:42:17-07:00","id":941681,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about this myself. I've got an Eleventh Question PC and I want to actually come up with some of the hypothetical questions that each Arcanum is the answer to.<br /> <br /> I would also note that nuggets of esoteric wisdom like this often have the quality of seeming simple or even trite at first read, but holding deeper significance to someone with experience of the thing, as if you're discovering it for the first time.<br /> <br /> Here's some quick ideas:<br /> <br /> Death: Nothing ends, and nothing is permanent. Everything can and will change. The greatest changes happen in darkness, unseen and unheard, but nothing can stay hidden in the dark forever.<br /> <br /> Space: All points are one. Separation disappears when points are considered from a different angle.<br /> <br /> Fate: Randomness is an illusion. Secret threads fully describe every event that happens, and those threads can be rewoven.<br /> <br /> Life: The quality of being alive is inherently metaphysically valuable. Vitality is agency. You have infinitely more in common with an amoeba than you do with your own reanimated corpse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:53:01-07:00","id":942078,"title":"","content":"Oh! I love thinking about this, I thought I was the only weirdo into it. I think of it in terms of Paths, though, since each Path is a revelation itself. So, I'm not sure about how I'd break these down into Arcana, but here are my takes on the central, transcendent truth of each Path:<br /> <br /> Obrimos: You are a face of the divine, a font of power. The Self is God; Brahman is Atman.<br /> Moros: You are both immortal and transient, an unwavering essence at the core of transmuting substance. The Self changes, but its essence remains.<br /> Acanthus: You are not bound except by yourself; your future is unwritten, your past your raw material. The Self is free of everything but itself.<br /> Mastigos: Your internal world is real, and changes within it can change the external world. The Self is a microcosm, reflecting and reflected by the macrocosm.<br /> Thyrsus: You are a part of nature, in communion with the world. The Self is not separate from the universe.<br /> <br /> As you can see, I take the Paths as together relating to a central Supernal revelation about the nature of humanity - that humans can matter and can change the world (for better or worse). This being the Supernal Truth of magecraft, and something the Exarchs would dearly like to quash. It also explains why the Lie seeks to suppress Supernal Truth, on an ideological rather than practical level.<br /> In theory, a master of every Arcana would internalize a complete understanding of that mystic revelation, I suppose, though being a 10-fold 10-arcanum grandmaster would be a bit far to go in practical terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}